\**{c=red:Note:}** **Dawn** is the final Mission of the {p:Chains of Promathia} storyline; however, the stories of {p:Chains of Promathia} and {p:Rise of the Zilart} are continued with the questline beginning with {q:Storms of Fate|Storms of Fate|Storms of Fate}.
=2 Walkthrough
* Zone into {z:The Garden of Ru'Hmet} and pass through the **Cermet Portal** to get to the main Garden elevator.
** Use the {p:Home Point} you obtained earlier selecting, Home Point #1 of {z:The Garden of Ru'Hmet}.
* Choose to descend to zone into {p:Empyreal Paradox}.
* Check the **Transcendental Radiance** for a cutscene and then check it again to enter the "**Dawn**" Battleground.

=2 Boss Fight
__This fight was initially uncapped at level 75. Level 99 players should have little to no difficulty with this mission.__
* See final cutscenes below to receive your ring after beating {m:Promathia}.
* {p:Prishe} joins you for this fight.
** {p:Prishe} can be healed if she takes damage.
** If she's KO'd, you can cast {p:Raise} on her and she will resume fighting with full HP and no weakness.
** {p:Prishe} will eat an {i:Ambrosia|Ambrosia|4511} when you start to fight.
** {p:Prishe} uses a {i:Daedalus Wing|Daedalus Wing|4202} when you start to fight.
** {p:Prishe} uses the Weapon Skill Auroral Uppercut.
** {p:Prishe} can casts {s:Divine Magic} on {m:Promathia} and {p:Cure} both herself and the party.
* Selh'teus joins you for this fight as well.
** Selh'teus cannot be healed by players, but has several abilities he can use to heal himself.
** Uses the Weapon skill **Luminous Lance**, which does a bit of damage and stuns {m:Promathia}.
** **If Selh'teus is KO'd, the battle immediately ends in failure.**
* **If the entire party is KO'd at any point during the fight, you will be immediately removed from the battlefield.**
* {m:Promathia} has low evasion and is immune to {s:Stun}.
* {m:Promathia} has two forms. Once you beat the first form, you can rest before engaging the second form.
** After a short period of time, {p:Prishe} will engage.

[Area
{p:Empyreal Paradox}
>Boss
{m:Promathia}
>Abilities
>**First form:**
* **Empty Salvation:** AOE damage (~250) and {s:Dispel} 3 effects
* **Pestilent Penance:** Cone Attack damage (~400) and {p:Plague}
* **Malevolent Blessing:** Cone Attack damage (400-500) and {p:Curse}
* **Infernal Deliverance:** AOE damage and {s:Stun}, ignores {p:Utsusemi}
* **Chains of (Apathy, Arrogance, Cowardice, Envy and Rage):**
** No effect on players due to the protection of the Light(s) of Holla/Dem/Mea/Vahzl/Al'Taieu.
** Inflicts terror on Alter Egos based on their race (i.e., Chains of Cowardice works on Tarutaru).
* **Comet (Spell):** Single-target magic damage (600-900). Can be absorbed by {p:Utsusemi}.

>**Second form:**
* It retains all its special attacks from the first form with the exception of Comet.
* **Seal of Quiescence:** AoE {p:Mute}, lasts up to 75 seconds.
** Cannot be curred by {s:Silena} or {i:Echo Drops|Echo Drops|4151}.
* **Winds of Oblivion:** AoE {p:Amnesia}, lasts up to 75 seconds.
* **Meteor (spell):** AoE magic damage (300-600)
** He casts this once a minute.
* **Bastion of Twilight:** Magic Shield effect.
* **Wheel of Impregnability:** {p:Invincible}.

>Notes
* {m:Promathia}'s first form has about 8000 HP.
* {m:Promathia}'s second form has about 12000 HP.
* You can tell which shield is up by looking at the ring below {m:Promathia}.
** Red is physical, green is magic.
* {p:Prishe} now uses the Weapon Skill **Nullifying Dropkick**, which breaks {m:Promathia}'s shields.
* Eventually, {p:Prishe} will use {p:Hundred Fists}.
* She can also use {p:Benediction} if she's in trouble.
* Selh'teus continues to fight against the second form.
** If his HP gets low he can use the Weapon Skill **Redemption** which gives HP, MP, and TP to him and any party members that may be near him.

